// TEST: Field Double Bound Spec
// ============================================================================
// The two bound spellings coexist but may not be combined ON ONE FIELD. This
// is a parse-time refusal with the caret on the `in`.
//
// It is worth an error rather than a precedence rule because the two
// spellings differ in INCLUSIVITY — `in 0 .. 3` is half-open and `min=0` is
// inclusive — so any silent winner would be a silent off-by-one for whichever
// spelling the reader was thinking in. There is no defensible default, so the
// language declines to pick one and says so.
// ============================================================================
struct Bad3 {
    m: Int<min=0> in 0 .. 3
}
// ERROR: BL1999
// ERROR-CONTAINS: has two bound specifications
